                  "owner_plan_id": "PLAN-bed480ce3e404b2cbaf5514d80a7f941",
                  "owner_revision": 1
                },
                {
                  "kind": "state",
                  "definition_id": "retained-scenario-audit",
                  "owner_plan_id": "PLAN-bed480ce3e404b2cbaf5514d80a7f941",
                  "owner_revision": 1
                }
              ],
              "parts": [
                {
                  "kind": "domain_rules",
                  "applicability": "applicable",
                  "rationale": "The controller owns irreversible reward decisions and their presentation.",
                  "responsibilities": [
                    "Implement the three legal complete journal states, single atomic durable append from empty and immutability after decision.",
                    "Attach grant, permanent decline and single logical map return to the durable decision transition. Preserve their counts during rendering and restoration.",
                    "Maintain isolated journals, serial calls, nonoverlapping processes and the specified storage-success assumption."
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "csharp_adapter",
                  "applicability": "not_applicable",
                  "rationale": "Implementation language remains delegated by the language-neutral synthetic interface specification.",
                  "responsibilities": []
                },
                {
                  "kind": "binding",
                  "applicability": "applicable",
                  "rationale": "Controller and harness require consistent executable, channel and runtime identity bindings.",
                  "responsibilities": [
                    "Implement and document the selected exclusive-reward-jsonl version 1 launch/message profile and exact acknowledgement return path.",
                    "Bind instance tokens to owned OS handles and J, retain ordered C through EOF and implement exact one-shot append barriers.",
                    "Provide synthetic lifecycle and business interfaces with distinct command dispatch and monotonic deadline handling."
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "kind": "scene",
                  "applicability": "applicable",
                  "rationale": "Startup and completed calls require independent observations of rendered UI.",
                  "responsibilities": [
                    "Render initial Idle for every process and journal-selected Idle, MapReady or MapCancelled before ordinary Complete.",
                    "Provide deterministic visible indicators and recognition regions for read-only OS surface capture.",
                    "Keep presentation and restoration free of repeated decision effects and logical returns."
                  ]
                }
              ],
              "observable_result": "The planned controller and harness resolve each scenario reward through an immutable journal decision and automatic presentation. Downstream verification must establish the eleven scenario outcomes, independent observations, final normal exits and complete retained audits.",
              "verification_targets": [
                "For every separate scenario provision a distinct newly empty J and fixed R. Preserve J across replacements, serialize calls and prevent process overlap. Verify J is always empty, [Commit(R)] or [Cancel(R)], permits one atomic durable append from empty and becomes immutable when decided. Apply successful storage except at the prescribed injected append barriers.",
                "At the domain decision boundary verify one grant and one logical map return for Commit, permanent decline with zero grants and one logical map return for Cancel, and unchanged effect counts during every render or restore. Every issued business call uses a fresh retained id and a guard that reads complete J. All empty, repeated and opposing-command branches progress automatically.",
                "For every start(J), begin a separate 10000ms deadline on the harness monotonic clock. Require matching live owned i/J, actual readUI(i)=Idle, complete readJ(J) equal to retained J and one timely matching Ready emitted after opening J and binding all three entry points. Complete these checks before any business call. Continue Ready auditing through EOF and require exactly one correct Ready already observed by the original startup deadline.",
                "For an ordinary call record CallStart immediately before issue. Within the same original 10000ms receive its matching Complete, then independently read actual rendered UI and every durable record while UI/J remain unchanged and before another call or lifecycle control. Check instance/id, reported versus actual UI, expected complete J, count observed so far and elapsed time. Record ObservationComplete only after all checks within that deadline. Treat progression as provisional through final EOF audits.",
                "For a hook call record CallStart once before armHook. Receive exactly one matching HookArmed on C before issuing the selected accept/cancel target. Require exactly one matching HookHit within the same original 10000ms including arming, acknowledgement and issue. Before blocks after the empty guard and before append. After blocks after durable append and before finalization or Complete. Keep all work blocked until immediate owned-process OS termination. The harness never releases a barrier. Audit exact identities, uniqueness, ordering and timing through EOF. Count only Complete as a completion and require zero for the crash target.",
                "For every shutdown or termination start a separate 10000ms exit deadline and require both the signaled owned OS handle and C EOF/drain. Shutdown sends Shutdown on Q and termination targets exactly owned i through the OS. Retain every issued id and event through drain. Require exactly one Complete per non-crashing invocation and zero per injected target. Preserve earlier invocation obligations across replacement processes.",
                "Latch missing, wrong, mismatched, duplicate or late results and all deadline failures. Reject duplicates arriving after ObservationComplete and Ready defects discovered after startup confirmation. Preserve startup failure after a late Ready and preserve any failure after a later crash, restart or cleanup. Failed-test cleanup contributes zero scenario coverage.",
                "Two accepts uses a separate fresh J. Both calls must observe [Commit(R)] and MapReady. Final invocation counts are [1,1], grants 1, permanent declines 0 and logical returns 1.",
                "Two cancels uses a separate fresh J. Both calls must observe [Cancel(R)] and MapCancelled. Final invocation counts are [1,1], grants 0, permanent declines 1 and logical returns 1.",
                "Accept then cancel uses a separate fresh J. Both calls must observe [Commit(R)] and MapReady. Final invocation counts are [1,1], grants 1, permanent declines 0 and logical returns 1.",
                "Cancel then accept uses a separate fresh J. Both calls must observe [Cancel(R)] and MapCancelled. Final invocation counts are [1,1], grants 0, permanent declines 1 and logical returns 1.",
                "Empty resume uses a separate fresh J. Resume must observe empty J and Idle. Its final invocation count is [1], with zero grants, permanent declines and logical returns.",
