                "RQ-b5ce45a545254d1a8aa205a5944535e3",
                "RQ-b0dfd40c17bb4789ab08cf31f920ecb9"
              ],
              "responsibility": "Own durable scenario J with exactly empty, [Commit(R)] or [Cancel(R)] as its complete value. Provision a different empty J and fixed R per scenario and retain J throughout that scenario. Permit one atomic durable append from empty and make decided J immutable. Commit supplies one grant and one logical map return. Cancel supplies permanent decline, zero grants and one logical map return. Couple effects to the durable transition so after-append crashes retain the decision and its effects while recovery rendering preserves their counts. Apply the specified storage-success assumption. Before crashes leave empty J and after crashes leave exactly the target record.",
              "uses": []
            },
            {
              "id": "rendered-map-ui",
              "requirement_ids": [
                "RQ-9f1d67605e48444881eb0329c233d880",
                "RQ-3c078fbc9c484aea935ef1c955c6b3ab",
                "RQ-4be0664a370442e6aefcd3b3d1556131"
              ],
              "responsibility": "Own volatile rendered UI. Every process initially shows Idle. Ordinary finalization automatically renders Idle for empty J, MapReady for Commit or MapCancelled for Cancel before Complete. Repeated accept after Commit and cancel after Commit preserve MapReady and the grant. Repeated cancel after Cancel and accept after Cancel preserve MapCancelled and permanent decline. Keep UI/J unchanged during independent post-completion reads. Preserve established business-effect and logical-return counts during presentation and restoration.",
              "uses": [
                {
                  "kind": "state",
                  "definition_id": "decision-journal",
                  "owner_plan_id": "PLAN-bed480ce3e404b2cbaf5514d80a7f941",
                  "owner_revision": 1
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "retained-scenario-audit",
              "requirement_ids": [
                "RQ-4be0664a370442e6aefcd3b3d1556131",
                "RQ-19d7f5e27dcd4a1d9236315f6bf288e3",
                "RQ-b5ce45a545254d1a8aa205a5944535e3",
                "RQ-b0dfd40c17bb4789ab08cf31f920ecb9"
              ],
              "responsibility": "Retain scenario reward/journal bindings, owned handles and instance tokens, every fresh issued call id, ordered per-instance C events and receipt times, startup/call/exit clock origins, independent observations, ObservationComplete markers, final event counts and latched failures. Preserve the ledger across ordinary restart and crash recovery. Continue Ready, hook and completion audits through each EOF/drain. Require one Complete per ordinary invocation, zero per crash target and exactly one correct Ready already observed by its startup deadline. Preserve failures detected after provisional progression, late Ready, later crashes and cleanup. Scenario acceptance includes final normal exit and complete audits, and failed-test cleanup receives zero coverage credit.",
              "uses": []
            }
