        "responsibility": "Implement synthetic start(J), readUI(i), readJ(J), shutdown(i), terminate(i), monotonic deadlines and retained auditing. Own OS handles, fresh Q/C and ordered per-instance event retention. start launches the controlled executable with J and endpoints and returns owned i. Independently confirm live i/J, timely Ready, actual Idle and every durable record equal to retained J within 10000ms from start, gating all business calls. readUI probes actual rendered output through read-only OS surface capture and readJ independently enumerates every durable record. Ordinary CallStart occurs immediately before issue. Hook CallStart occurs once before armHook. Complete all non-crashing completion, stable independent UI/J, identity, count-so-far and deadline checks and ObservationComplete within the original 10000ms. Retain every issued id and failure through all instance EOF/drains and replacements. Require final Complete counts of one per non-crashing invocation and zero per crash target. Continue exact Ready and hook audits through EOF and reject late duplicates after provisional progression. shutdown sends Shutdown on Q. terminate targets exactly owned i through the OS. Each begins a separate 10000ms exit deadline requiring signaled handle and C EOF/drain. Inspect complete crash J before replacement. Ordinary restart follows successful observations, normal shutdown, confirmed exit/EOF, replacement start, confirmed startup and fresh-id resume. Crash recovery follows immediate hook termination, confirmed exit/EOF, unchanged-J replacement and ordinary resume. End every scenario with final normal exit and full audits. Preserve all failures and earlier invocation obligations across crashes, replacements and cleanup. The scenario verification implementer must use these operations for all eleven scenarios and retain their execution evidence.",
