        "responsibility": "Implement and document the inherited draft-selected exclusive-reward-jsonl version 1 profile for shared controller/harness use. Launch spelling is controlled-executable --profile exclusive-reward-jsonl --profile-version 1 --journal <journal-path> --instance <instance-token> --control <Q-name> --events <C-name>. The harness creates fresh named-pipe Q/C endpoints for each process and binds a fresh runtime instance token to owned OS handle i and canonical J. Wire i carries that token. Supply a lossless reward handle bound identically to fixed scenario R. Each frame is a UTF-8 JSON object followed by LF with JSON escaping preserving strings. Every frame carries version=1, type and i. Q is harness-to-controller and C is controller-to-harness. Q accept, cancel and resume carry version,type,i,R,id. Q armHook carries version,type,i,id,op,phase with op accept or cancel and phase before or after. Q Shutdown carries version,type,i. C Ready carries version,type,i,J. C Complete carries version,type,i,id,ui with ui Idle, MapReady or MapCancelled. C HookArmed and HookHit carry version,type,i,id,op,phase. HookArmed on C is the exact armHook acknowledgement and precedes target issue. Install its one-shot hook only for the selected id/op while J is empty. Before emits and flushes HookHit after the empty guard and blocks before atomic append. After emits and flushes HookHit after durable append and blocks before UI finalization or Complete. Block all work until OS termination with the harness never releasing the barrier. CallStart begins once before armHook, includes acknowledgement and issue and stays unchanged. Require exactly one matching HookArmed and HookHit within the original 10000ms, then immediately terminate the owned process. Keep hooks disabled for every other call. Audit HookArmed and HookHit separately and count only Complete as completion. Open J, bind all three business entry points and render initial Idle before exactly one Ready. Render ordinary outcomes before Complete. Retain ordered C frames and monotonic receipt times through EOF/drain. Malformed frames, wrong versions and unexpected, missing, duplicate, late or mismatched events latch failure. Preserve source event identities, command distinctions, ordering, blocked barriers, independent observations, retained counts, deadlines and scenarios. Resolve and document any selected profile revision before downstream plan completion.",
